3. THE BOUNDARY — anchors are end-of-day — PASS (independently mutation-tested)

CODE (balance.go:60-65):
    txDay := dayOf(tx.Date)
    if txDay.After(anchorDay) && !txDay.After(atDay) {
        sum += tx.Amount
    }
This is the half-open window (anchorDay, atDay] required by GLOSSARY.md:124-131
and spec §4 ("plus the sum of that account's transaction amounts in
(anchor.Date, date]"). dayOf() (balance.go:197-199) truncates to the calendar
day in the same location, so the comparison is day-granular and the anchor's
own time component cannot leak a same-day transaction in.

I did NOT take the worker's mutation claim on trust. I re-derived it by
mutating the comparison myself and running the suite. The mutants live in the
scratchpad and were injected with `go test -overlay=<scratch>/overlay.json`,
which substitutes the file in-memory at compile time — nothing was ever
written into the worktree (integrity confirmed in item 9 below).

M1 — the exact off-by-one under suspicion: `txDay.After(anchorDay)` changed to
`!txDay.Before(anchorDay)` (i.e. `>`  becomes `>=`, inclusive of the anchor
day). KILLED by assertion, and it produced precisely the double-counted value:
    --- FAIL: TestBalanceAt_AnchorDayTransactionIsExcluded
        balance_test.go:120: Amount = 4810.0000, want 4310.0000 (same-day tx must be excluded from the anchor)
        balance_test.go:128: Amount matched the off-by-one value 4810.00; the anchor-day transaction was double-counted
    --- FAIL: TestBalanceAt_AnchorDayTransactionExcludedEvenWithTimeComponent
        balance_test.go:159: Amount = 1350.0000, want 1100.0000 (same-day 23:59 tx must be excluded from the anchor)
    --- FAIL: TestBalanceAt_AnchorExactlyOnAtIsIncluded
        balance_test.go:262: Amount = 2777.0000, want 2000.00 (same-day tx excluded, anchor stands)
THREE independent tests fail on the inclusive boundary. The worker's claim is
confirmed as truthful: the tests genuinely discriminate `>` from `>=`. They do
not pass vacuously and they are not tautological — the 4810.00 value the
assertion names is the real double-counted balance the mutant computes.

TIME-COMPONENT CASE (explicitly required): M2b replaced the day-granular
anchor comparison with a full-timestamp one (`tx.Date.After(anchor.Date)`).
First attempt died on a compile error (unused `anchorDay`), which is NOT a
valid kill, so I repaired the mutant with a blank assignment and re-ran:
    --- FAIL: TestBalanceAt_AnchorDayTransactionExcludedEvenWithTimeComponent
        balance_test.go:159: Amount = 1350.0000, want 1100.0000 (same-day 23:59 tx must be excluded from the anchor)
balance_test.go:138-161 pins anchor at 2026-08-01 09:00 and a transaction at
2026-08-01 23:59; the 23:59 row is correctly excluded (1000 + 100 = 1100, not
1350). Requirement met.

