6. DRIFT SEMANTICS — the asymmetry — PASS
balance.go:136: `if txDay.After(earlierDay) && !txDay.After(laterDay)`.
Earlier anchor's own day EXCLUDED, later anchor's own day INCLUDED — the same
(earlier, later] window shape as BalanceAt, which is what makes Predicted and
Actual comparable (the later anchor is end-of-day, so it already reflects its
own day's rows and the prediction must too).

Both edges of the asymmetry are pinned by TestDrift_MissingRowsBetweenAnchors
(balance_test.go:327-371), which deliberately plants a row on EACH anchor day
(8/1 = 50.00 excluded, 8/15 = 200.00 included). I mutated each edge separately:

M6 — later anchor's day wrongly EXCLUDED (`!After(laterDay)` -> `Before(laterDay)`). KILLED:
    --- FAIL: TestDrift_MissingRowsBetweenAnchors
        balance_test.go:363: Predicted = 1100.0000, want 1300.00 (1000 + 100 + 200; 8/1 tx excluded, 8/15 tx included)
        balance_test.go:369: Difference = 400.0000, want 200.00 (Actual - Predicted)

M7 — earlier anchor's day wrongly INCLUDED (`After(earlierDay)` -> `!Before(earlierDay)`). KILLED:
    --- FAIL: TestDrift_MissingRowsBetweenAnchors
        balance_test.go:363: Predicted = 1350.0000, want 1300.00 (1000 + 100 + 200; 8/1 tx excluded, 8/15 tx included)
        balance_test.go:369: Difference = 150.0000, want 200.00 (Actual - Predicted)

Each edge fails in its own direction (1100 vs 1350 against the correct 1300),
so the test discriminates the asymmetry rather than merely the window width —
a symmetric-but-shifted window would not produce these two distinct failures.
Difference is Actual - Predicted (balance.go:141); a sign flip would yield -200
and fail balance_test.go:368.

M10 — Drift not sorting anchors. KILLED:
    --- FAIL: TestDrift_UnsortedAnchorsProducesSortedReports
        balance_test.go:509: From/To = 2026-08-15/2026-08-01, want 2026-08-01/2026-08-15

