7. FLOAT COMPARISON — PASS
`grep -n "==\|!=" internal/services/accounts/balance.go` returns only string
comparisons on tx.AccountID (:57, :83, :129) and one comment (:41). There is
NO float equality comparison anywhere in balance.go.
Epsilon convention: `floatTolerance = 1e-9` (balance.go:16), matching the
repo's existing convention — verified the cited precedent really exists:
    internal/services/retirement/guardrails_test.go:10:const floatTolerance = 1e-9
Tests compare money through moneyEq() (balance_test.go:15-17,
`math.Abs(a-b) < floatTolerance`), never with `==`.
Rounding is presentation-only: the only snap is Drift collapsing sub-epsilon
float dust to exact 0 (balance.go:146-148); Predicted and Actual are stored at
full precision and the sum accumulates in stored precision. No rounding occurs
inside BalanceAt's computation.

