9. ADDITIONAL DUE DILIGENCE

Ruling 2026-08-16e (vacuous loop assertions on an empty set): I checked every
loop-based assertion in the new tests. The only assertion loop is
balance_test.go:532 in TestBalanceAt_DoesNotMutateAnchors, iterating `before`,
which is a copy of a hard-coded 2-element literal (balance_test.go:522-528) —
it is not a set computed by the code under test and cannot be vacuously empty.
Every Drift test that indexes into `reports` has a `len(reports)` count
assertion in front of it (balance_test.go:354, 393, 417, 428, 457, 505), which
is exactly the guard that ruling demands. No vacuous-pass pattern found.

Ruling 2026-08-16a (tests passing while behavior was wrong): addressed head-on
by the mutation campaign above rather than by inspection alone. Ten mutants
across all three functions; every one that compiled was killed by a named
assertion. Three mutants (M2, M3, M8) initially died from BUILD failures
(unused variables) — I deliberately did not count those as kills, repaired
them, and re-ran to obtain genuine behavioral kills. Control run M0
(unmutated original through the identical overlay path) PASSES, proving the
harness is not simply failing everything.

